<article class="item" id="2026-11-22-pmid-43063989">
  <div class="tagrow"><span class="tag">鼻整形</span><span class="tag">人工智能</span><span class="tag">医患沟通</span></div>
  <h2><a href="https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/43063989/" rel="noopener">Multimodal AI for Rhinoplasty Consultation and Simulation: A Blinded Expert Evaluation</a></h2>
  <div class="journal">Facial Plastic Surgery · Hack S · PMID 43063989 · <a href="https://doi.org/10.1055/a-3003-2319" rel="noopener">doi</a><span class="affil">Sheba Medical Center, University of Nicosia, Tel HaShomer, Israel</span></div>
  <p class="line fact"><b>事实｜</b>20 例鼻整形患者照片，多模态人工智能生成咨询与术后模拟图；4 名盲法面整形医生按 12 项五分制评分。语言清晰度 4.05 分最高，术式适当性 2.90、方案与模拟一致性 2.33 分垫底；完全认可方案仅 7.6%。</p>
  <p class="line take"><b>点评｜</b>创新点：首次让盲法专家按患者逐个打分多模态人工智能的咨询文本与模拟图，而非只看图像是否逼真。意义：模拟图可作沟通工具，不能当术前承诺；方案必须由医生独立制定，接诊时先问患者是否拿人工智能图来对标。</p>
  <p class="en">Preoperative photographs from 20 rhinoplasty patients were used by a multimodal AI (GPT-5.5) to generate a consultation in a standardised patient-voiced prompt and a simulated postoperative image; four blinded fellowship-trained facial plastic surgeons rated each output on 12 five-point items, two utility items and one surgical-plan agreement item, with mixed models using crossed random effects for case and evaluator. Language clarity scored highest at 4.05/5, whereas procedure appropriateness (2.90), avoidance of inappropriate procedures (2.59) and plan-to-simulation fidelity (2.33) were lowest, and full agreement with the surgical plan occurred in only 7.6% of assessments. Its contribution is a blinded, per-patient item-by-item evaluation of both AI text and AI imagery rather than a judgement of how convincing the pictures look. Simulations can support conversation but cannot serve as a preoperative promise; the operative plan must remain the surgeon&#x27;s, and clinics should ask at consultation whether the patient is benchmarking against an AI-generated image.</p>
  <div class="comments"><p style="color:#8a8a8a;font-size:13px;margin:6px 0">还没有批注</p></div>
