<article class="item" id="2026-11-22-pmid-43062567">
  <div class="tagrow"><span class="tag">颅骨修复</span><span class="tag">系统综述</span><span class="tag">精神心理结局</span></div>
  <h2><a href="https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/43062567/" rel="noopener">Neuropsychiatric outcomes after decompressive craniectomy and cranioplasty: a systematic review and meta-analysis (systematic review)</a></h2>
  <div class="journal">Neurosurgical Review · Bari SSM · PMID 43062567 · <a href="https://doi.org/10.1007/s10143-026-04560-y" rel="noopener">doi</a><span class="affil">Department of Neurosurgery, Queen&#x27;s Hospital, Barking, Havering and Redbridge University Hospitals NHS Trust, London, UK</span></div>
  <p class="line fact"><b>事实｜</b>24 项研究、877 例去骨瓣减压患者的系统综述与 meta 分析，12 项、305 例入池：抑郁合并患病率 47%（95%CI 40–54%），焦虑 46%；两项纵向研究示颅骨修补后情绪改善，但样本小。</p>
  <p class="line take"><b>点评｜</b>创新点：首次把去骨瓣减压后的抑郁与焦虑做成合并患病率，量化到接近一半。意义：颅骨修补不能只谈外形与脑保护，术前应常规筛情绪，把修补前后当作心理随访节点；文中效应量不宜直接引用，纵向证据仍薄。</p>
  <p class="en">This systematic review and meta-analysis pooled 24 studies (N=877) of patients after decompressive craniectomy, with 12 studies (N=305) in the quantitative synthesis. Pooled prevalence was 47% for depression (95% CI 40-54%) and 46% for anxiety (95% CI 38-54%); two longitudinal studies suggested reduced anxiety and depression 12 months after cranioplasty, although small cohorts may have inflated those effect sizes. Its contribution is the first pooled estimate of post-decompressive-craniectomy depression and anxiety, putting the burden near one in two patients. Cranioplasty should therefore be framed as more than contour and brain protection: screen mood before surgery and treat the repair as a psychological follow-up checkpoint, while citing the longitudinal effect sizes cautiously.</p>
  <div class="comments"><p style="color:#8a8a8a;font-size:13px;margin:6px 0">还没有批注</p></div>
